"""Compare existing demonstration artifacts. Never generates new compositions."""
import hashlib
import json
from pathlib import Path
from PIL import Image
from map_layout import ROOT
from playable_composition import compile_composition
from semantic_pipeline import digest

def read(p):return json.loads(p.read_text())

def main():
    out=ROOT/'output/specification-to-image-003';names=['compact','mid','interior'];data={n:{k:read(out/n/(k+'.json')) for k in ['composition','validation','summary','manifest']} for n in names}
    # Final sources match the sources actually exercised by these experiments.
    source_current={n:all(hashlib.sha256((ROOT/file).read_bytes()).hexdigest()==h for file,h in data[n]['manifest']['sources'].items()) for n in names}
    prior=read(ROOT/'output/p04-frozen-search-001/manifest.json');frozen_prior_unchanged=all(hashlib.sha256((ROOT/file).read_bytes()).hexdigest()==h for file,h in prior['source_hashes'].items())
    if not all(source_current.values()) or not frozen_prior_unchanged:raise ValueError('Source provenance check failed')
    for filename in ('clean.png','encounters.png'):
        im=Image.new('RGB',(2400,800),'#101923')
        for i,n in enumerate(names):im.paste(Image.open(out/n/filename).resize((800,800)),(800*i,0))
        im.save(out/('comparison-'+filename))
    programs={n:data[n]['composition'] for n in names};compiled={n:compile_composition(p) for n,p in programs.items()}
    evidence=dict(request_and_physical_passes={n:dict(physical=data[n]['validation']['physical_pass'],adherence=data[n]['validation']['request_pass']) for n in names},
         same_base_seed=271828,total_final_proposals=3,max_attempts_per_demo=4,
         courtyard_to_interior=dict(same_strategic_network=programs['compact']['strategic_network']==programs['interior']['strategic_network'],same_role_placement=programs['compact']['decision_log'][-1]['role_cells']==programs['interior']['decision_log'][-1]['role_cells'],changed_wall_area_plan_units=compiled['compact']['walls'].symmetric_difference(compiled['interior']['walls']).area,macro_diversity_claim=False),
         optional_Mid=dict(changed_walkable_area_plan_units=compiled['compact']['walkable'].symmetric_difference(compiled['mid']['walkable']).area,no_Mid_site_free_T_CT=data['compact']['validation']['site_free_T_CT_path'] is not None,Mid_site_free_T_CT=data['mid']['validation']['site_free_T_CT_path'] is not None,macro_connectivity_change=True),
         source_matches_current=source_current,frozen_P04_sources_unchanged=frozen_prior_unchanged,
         independent_snapshot_replay_matches=digest(read(out/'replay-compact/composition.json'))==digest(programs['compact']),
         diversity_evaluation='Two connectivity organizations demonstrated. Courtyard/interior is a local architecture comparison, not a third macro family. All still inherit rectangular reservation and opposing deployment bias.',
         stage4_paused=True)
    (out/'comparison.json').write_text(json.dumps(evidence,indent=2))
    rows=[]
    for n in names:
        v=data[n]['validation'];p=programs[n];widths=v['opening_widths'];main=v['routes'];log=p['decision_log'][-1]
        rows.append(f'| {n} | {len(p["spaces"])} | {len(widths)} | {min(x["actual_HU"] for x in widths):.0f}–{max(x["actual_HU"] for x in widths):.0f} | {main["T-A-main"]["path"]["length_HU"]:.0f} | {main["T-B-main"]["path"]["length_HU"]:.0f} |')
    report=['# Specification-to-image demonstrations — candidates for review','', 'The direct JSON path is implemented end-to-end. Three final demonstrations, all using base/attempt seed 271828 and a four-attempt cap, passed physical and request checks on the first attempt. No candidate-specific coordinate edits. Stage 4 and engine geometry remain paused.','', '## Inspect the images','', '[Clean plans at identical scale: no Mid / contested Mid / interiors](comparison-clean.png)','', '[Corresponding route/encounter overlays](comparison-encounters.png)','', 'Individual 1600px plans and overlays are in compact/, mid/ and interior/. Pale lines are actual openings; full-height building masses are dark; 48-HU cover is tan; objective outlines identify plant areas. Overlay orange is main attack, pink secondary attack, blue defender traversal, green independent Mid approach, red sampled standing rays.','', '## What the request changed','', '| Request | Architectural/connectivity result | Evaluation |','|---|---|---|', '| Compact two-site, no Mid | Inaccessible center; independent main commitments, local alternative entries and rear receiving/deployment circulation. | Physical/request pass. Still has a long straight northern rear gallery and broad travel loop. |', '| Contested Mid, secondary access to both sites | Adds a real middle courtyard, independent T/CT approaches, distinct physical connectors to both objectives and a control-dependent central rotation. | Physical/request pass. Central contest and connector safety/timing are unresolved. Adds central connectivity rather than another site name. |', '| Same no-Mid request/seed, interior sites | Same roles and strategic route network; actual objective vestibules, full-height partitions and separate clearing thresholds replace the courts. | Physical/request pass. A controlled local change, not proof of another overall composition family. |','', 'The middle is optional. Neither P04 nor P01 is loaded as a map template. Shared architecture rules and their sampled assembly are the source of these layouts, not the trained neural model.','', '## Physical measurements','', '| Demo | Architectural spaces | Actual openings | Clear widths HU | Ordered T→A main HU | Ordered T→B main HU |','|---|---:|---:|---|---:|---:|']
    report+=rows
    report+=['', 'All three have one connected walkable component, required routes after provisional 32-HU player erosion, matching nominal/actual apertures, no sampled undeclared openings and physically different main/secondary site-complex door crossings. No-Mid has no site-free T→CT path; Mid explicitly permits a path through the contested middle and disallows a bypass with both sites and Mid blocked. These are bounded geometry/connectivity checks, not proof of effective tactical decisions.','', 'Ordered traversal distances describe requested architectural paths. Unrestricted shortest lengths are also saved per route in validation.json; players are not assumed to obey the intended traversal. 2D scale, standing/crouched eyes, speed and collision remain provisional. No timing in seconds or calibrated balance claims.','', '## Separate spatial diversity assessment','', evidence['diversity_evaluation'],'', f'The controlled interior comparison changes {evidence["courtyard_to_interior"]["changed_wall_area_plan_units"]:.1f} plan² of wall geometry while retaining roles and route selection. Mid changes {evidence["optional_Mid"]["changed_walkable_area_plan_units"]:.1f} plan² of actual walkable space and adds usable central connectivity.','', 'Remaining architectural weaknesses: the reservation scaffold favors orthogonal shapes; the no-Mid outer loop remains long; several holding/receiving rooms are regular and lightly developed; local objectives need visual judgment and more varied architecture. These images show functioning controls, not the finished professional-CS2-layout generator.','', '## Reproduce','', 'From repository root, using new output directories:','', '```powershell', '.tools\\training\\Scripts\\python.exe map_layout.py --spec config/map-spec-compact.json --seed 271828 --output output/my-compact --attempt-limit 4', '.tools\\training\\Scripts\\python.exe map_layout.py --spec config/map-spec-mid.json --seed 271828 --output output/my-mid --attempt-limit 4', '.tools\\training\\Scripts\\python.exe map_layout.py --spec config/map-spec-interior.json --seed 271828 --output output/my-interior --attempt-limit 4', '```','', 'Frozen-source replay:', '', '```powershell', '.tools\\training\\Scripts\\python.exe output/specification-to-image-003/compact/source/map_layout.py --spec output/specification-to-image-003/compact/specification.json --output output/replay-from-snapshot --attempt-limit 4', '```','', 'Each selected composition was regenerated from scratch and its full composition/decision hash matched. The independent frozen-source compact replay also matched. Source hashes for these final demonstrations still match current code; frozen P04 search sources remain unchanged.','', '## Failure/adapter evidence','', '[Bounded failure report](../specification-to-image-001/bounded-failure/failure-report.json) · [Diagnostic image](../specification-to-image-001/bounded-failure/diagnostic.png)','', 'The deliberately too-short 256-HU complete-main-route cap rejected both attempts; no relaxation or accepted clean plan was returned. A separate missing-credential invocation saved [the explicit prompt-unavailable report](../specification-to-image-001/prompt-unavailable/failure-report.json). There is no keyword parser.','', 'The Responses/Structured Outputs adapter is implemented and unit-tested using injected responses/refusals/unsupported requests; no live LLM interpretation was possible without OPENAI_API_KEY and an accessible model supplied via --model. See specification-to-image.md for enablement and supported controls. JSON mode requires no API.','', '## Tests and prior evidence','', '49 combined pipeline/compiler/P04 regression tests passed before the final investment control addition. The final 13 specification/pipeline tests then passed, including staged physical investment, geometry-controlled interiors, real Mid connectivity, invalid specifications, blocked Mid, aperture interference, bounded failure, determinism and adapter refusal. Tests are implementation evidence, not quality evidence.','', 'Earlier development rounds spec-layout-demo-r1..r5 and spec-layout-demo-final, plus specification-to-image-001/002, are retained with source snapshots and failures. The cellular first render, validator bugs, partition/frontage failures and actual-ingress correction are documented in specification-to-image.md. The frozen P04 search and all earlier authored outputs are preserved. No further P04-only seed searches occurred.','', 'This implementation and bounded demonstration experiment is complete and stopped for review.']
    (out/'review.md').write_text('\n'.join(report),encoding='utf-8')
    policy_path=ROOT/'generation-policy.json';policy=read(policy_path);policy.update(p04_only_seed_searches_stopped=True,stage_3_review='output/specification-to-image-003/review.md',stage_3_experiment_status='specification_to_image_demonstrations_complete',stage_3_specification_experiment=dict(output='output/specification-to-image-003',seed=271828,demonstrations=names,completed=True),geometry_paused=True,stage_4_authorized=False,stage_3_batch_authorized=False);policy_path.write_text(json.dumps(policy,indent=2)+'\n')
    print(json.dumps(evidence,indent=2))

if __name__=='__main__':main()
